k-pr-title CI validation Supports multiple PR types, including feat, fix, and perf Automates PR creation using a standardized title format Integrates with GitHub for seamless workflow automation create-pr is a GitHub pull request automation skill that formats titles according to the required <type>(<scope>): <summary> format, ensuring compliance with n8n''s CI validation rules.');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('obra/superpowers/test-driven-development', 'official', 'obra', 'superpowers', 'obra/superpowers', 'test-driven-development', 71924, 5546, 86, '2026-03-06T03:26:30Z', '2026-03-06T03:35:19.586Z', '7dee67b4af6bdccc7a914ca34533184d64592d0f5b23aeae631538168db14994', '{"id":"obra/superpowers/test-driven-development","name":"test-driven-development","description":{"en":"Test-driven development is a process for implementing features and bug fixes by writing tests first. It benefits developers by ensuring code quality and reliability.","es":"El Desarrollo Dirigido por Pruebas (TDD) es una técnica de desarrollo de software que implica escribir pruebas antes de implementar el código. Esto ayuda a garantizar la calidad y reducir errores","fr":"Le Développement Piloté par les Tests (TDD) est une technique de développement logiciel qui consiste à écrire des tests avant de mettre en œuvre le code. Cela aide à garantir la qualité et à réduire les erreurs","de":"Die testgetriebene Entwicklung (TDD) ist eine Software-Entwicklungstechnik, bei der Tests vor der Implementierung des Codes geschrieben werden. Dies hilft, die Qualität zu gewährleisten und Fehler zu reduzieren","pt":"O desenvolvimento dirigido por testes (TDD) é uma prática de codificação que envolve escrever testes antes de escrever o código de implementação.","ru":"Test-Driven Development (TDD) - это методология программирования, при которой сначала пишутся тесты, а затем код реализации.","ar":"التطوير الموجه بالاختبار (TDD) هو منهجية برمجة تتضمن كتابة الاختبارات قبل كتابة رمز التنفيذ."},"owner":"obra","repo":"superpowers","repoPath":"obra/superpowers","stars":71924,"forks":5546,"updatedAt":"2026-03-06T03:26:30Z","topics":[],"skillMd":{"name":"test-driven-development","description":"Use when implementing any feature or bugfix, before writing implementation code","bodyPreview":"# Test-Driven Development (TDD)\n\n## Overview\n\nWrite the test first. Watch it fail. Write minimal code to pass.\n\n**Core principle:** If you didn''t watch the test fail, you don''t know if it tests the right thing.\n\n**Violating the letter of the rules is violating the spirit of the rules.**\n\n## When to Use\n\n**Always:**\n- New features\n- Bug fixes\n- Refactoring\n- Behavior changes\n\n**Exceptions (ask your human partner):**\n- Throwaway prototypes\n- Generated code\n- Configuration files\n\nThinking \"skip TDD","body":"# Test-Driven Development (TDD)\n\n## Overview\n\nWrite the test first. Watch it fail. Write minimal code to pass.\n\n**Core principle:** If you didn''t watch the test fail, you don''t know if it tests the right thing.\n\n**Violating the letter of the rules is violating the spirit of the rules.**\n\n## When to Use\n\n**Always:**\n- New features\n- Bug fixes\n- Refactoring\n- Behavior changes\n\n**Exceptions (ask your human partner):**\n- Throwaway prototypes\n- Generated code\n- Configuration files\n\nThinking \"skip TDD just this once\"? Stop. That''s rationalization.\n\n## The Iron Law\n\n```\nNO PRODUCTION CODE WITHOUT A FAILING TEST FIRST\n```\n\nWrite code before the test? Delete it. Start over.\n\n**No exceptions:**\n- Don''t keep it as \"reference\"\n- Don''t \"adapt\" it while writing tests\n- Don''t look at it\n- Delete means delete\n\nImplement fresh from tests. Period.\n\n## Red-Green-Refactor\n\n```dot\ndigraph tdd_cycle {\n    rankdir=LR;\n    red [label=\"RED\\nWrite failing test\", shape=box, style=filled, fillcolor=\"#ffcccc\"];\n    verify_red [label=\"Verify fails\\ncorrectly\", shape=diamond];\n    green [label=\"GREEN\\nMinimal code\", shape=box, style=filled, fillcolor=\"#ccffcc\"];\n    verify_green [label=\"Verify passes\\nAll green\", shape=diamond];\n    refactor [label=\"REFACTOR\\nClean up\", shape=box, style=filled, fillcolor=\"#ccccff\"];\n    next [label=\"Next\", shape=ellipse];\n\n    red -> verify_red;\n    verify_red -> green [label=\"yes\"];\n    verify_red -> red [label=\"wrong\\nfailure\"];\n    green -> verify_green;\n    verify_green -> refactor [label=\"yes\"];\n    verify_green -> green [label=\"no\"];\n    refactor -> verify_green [label=\"stay\\ngreen\"];\n    verify_green -> next;\n    next -> red;\n}\n```\n\n### RED - Write Failing Test\n\nWrite one minimal test showing what should happen.\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\ntest(''retries failed operations 3 times'', async () => {\n  let attempts = 0;\n  const operation = () => {\n    attempts++;\n    if (attempts < 3) throw new Error(''fail'');\n    return ''success'';\n  };\n\n  const result = await retryOperation(operation);\n\n  expect(result).toBe(''success'');\n  expect(attempts).toBe(3);\n});\n```\nClear name, tests real behavior, one thing\n</Good>\n\n<Bad>\n```typescript\ntest(''retry works'', async () => {\n  const mock = jest.fn()\n    .mockRejectedValueOnce(new Error())\n    .mockRejectedValueOnce(new Error())\n    .mockResolvedValueOnce(''success'');\n  await retryOperation(mock);\n  expect(mock).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(3);\n});\n```\nVague name, tests mock not code\n</Bad>\n\n**Requirements:**\n- One behavior\n- Clear name\n- Real code (no mocks unless unavoidable)\n\n### Verify RED - Watch It Fail\n\n**MANDATORY. Never skip.**\n\n```bash\nnpm test path/to/test.test.ts\n```\n\nConfirm:\n- Test fails (not errors)\n- Failure message is expected\n- Fails because feature missing (not typos)\n\n**Test passes?** You''re testing existing behavior. Fix test.\n\n**Test errors?** Fix error, re-run until it fails correctly.\n\n### GREEN - Minimal Code\n\nWrite simplest code to pass the test.\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\nasync function retryOperation<T>(fn: () => Promise<T>): Promise<T> {\n  for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) {\n    try {\n      return await fn();\n    } catch (e) {\n      if (i === 2) throw e;\n    }\n  }\n  throw new Error(''unreachable'');\n}\n```\nJust enough to pass\n</Good>\n\n<Bad>\n```typescript\nasync function retryOperation<T>(\n  fn: () => Promise<T>,\n  options?: {\n    maxRetries?: number;\n    backoff?: ''linear'' | ''exponential'';\n    onRetry?: (attempt: number) => void;\n  }\n): Promise<T> {\n  // YAGNI\n}\n```\nOver-engineered\n</Bad>\n\nDon''t add features, refactor other code, or \"improve\" beyond the test.\n\n### Verify GREEN - Watch It Pass\n\n**MANDATORY.**\n\n```bash\nnpm test path/to/test.test.ts\n```\n\nConfirm:\n- Test passes\n- Other tests still pass\n- Output pristine (no errors, warnings)\n\n**Test fails?** Fix code, not test.\n\n**Other tests fail?** Fix now.\n\n### REFACTOR - Clean Up\n\nAfter green only:\n- Remove duplication\n- Improve names\n- Extract helpers\n\nKeep tests green. Don''t add behavior.\n\n### Repeat\n\nNext failing test for next feature.\n\n## Good Tests\n\n| Quality | Good | Bad |\n|---------|------|-----|\n| **Minimal** | One thing. \"and\" in name? Split it. | `test(''validates email and domain and whitespace'')` |\n| **Clear** | Name describes behavior | `test(''test1'')` |\n| **Shows intent** | Demonstrates desired API | Obscures what code should do |\n\n## Why Order Matters\n\n**\"I''ll write tests after to verify it works\"**\n\nTests written after code pass immediately. Passing immediately proves nothing:\n- Might test wrong thing\n- Might test implementation, not behavior\n- Might miss edge cases you forgot\n- You never saw it catch the bug\n\nTest-first forces you to see the test fail, proving it actually tests something.\n\n**\"I already manually tested all the edge cases\"**\n\nManual testing is ad-hoc. You think you tested everything but:\n- No record of what you tested\n- Can''t re-run when code changes\n- Easy to forget cases under pressure\n- \"It worked when I tried it\" ≠ comprehensive\n\nAutomated tests are systematic. They run the same way every time.\n\n**\"Deleting X hours of work is wasteful\"**\n\nSunk cost fallacy. The time is already gone. Your choice now:\n- Delete and rewrite with TDD (X more hours, high confidence)\n- Keep it and add tests after (30 min, low confidence, likely bugs)\n\nThe \"waste\" is keeping code you can''t trust. Working code without real tests is technical debt.\n\n**\"TDD is dogmatic, being pragmatic means adapting\"**\n\nTDD IS pragmatic:\n- Finds bugs before commit (faster than debugging after)\n- Prevents regressions (tests catch breaks immediately)\n- Documents behavior (tests show how to use code)\n- Enables refactoring (change freely, tests catch breaks)\n\n\"Pragmatic\" shortcuts = debugging in production = slower.\n\n**\"Tests after achieve the same goals - it''s spirit not ritual\"**\n\nNo. Tests-after answer \"What does this do?\" Tests-first answer \"What should this do?\"\n\nTests-after are biased by your implementation. You test what you built, not what''s required. You verify remembered edge cases, not discovered ones.\n\nTests-first force edge case discovery before implementing. Tests-after verify you remembered everything (you didn''t).\n\n30 minutes of tests after ≠ TDD. You get coverage, lose proof tests work.\n\n## Common Rationalizations\n\n| Excuse | Reality |\n|--------|---------|\n| \"Too simple to test\" | Simple code breaks. Test takes 30 seconds. |\n| \"I''ll test after\" | Tests passing immediately prove nothing. |\n| \"Tests after achieve same goals\" | Tests-after = \"what does this do?\" Tests-first = \"what should this do?\" |\n| \"Already manually tested\" | Ad-hoc ≠ systematic. No record, can''t re-run. |\n| \"Deleting X hours is wasteful\" | Sunk cost fallacy. Keeping unverified code is technical debt. |\n| \"Keep as reference, write tests first\" | You''ll adapt it. That''s testing after. Delete means delete. |\n| \"Need to explore first\" | Fine. Throw away exploration, start with TDD. |\n| \"Test hard = design unclear\" | Listen to test. Hard to test = hard to use. |\n| \"TDD will slow me down\" | TDD faster than debugging. Pragmatic = test-first. |\n| \"Manual test faster\" | Manual doesn''t prove edge cases. You''ll re-test every change. |\n| \"Existing code has no tests\" | You''re improving it. Add tests for existing code. |\n\n## Red Flags - STOP and Start Over\n\n- Code before test\n- Test after implementation\n- Test passes immediately\n- Can''t explain why test failed\n- Tests added \"later\"\n- Rationalizing \"just this once\"\n- \"I already manually tested it\"\n- \"Tests after achieve the same purpose\"\n- \"It''s about spirit not ritual\"\n- \"Keep as reference\" or \"adapt existing code\"\n- \"Already spent X hours, deleting is wasteful\"\n- \"TDD is dogmatic, I''m being pragmatic\"\n- \"This is different because...\"\n\n**All of these mean: Delete code. Start over with TDD.**\n\n## Example: Bug Fix\n\n**Bug:** Empty email accepted\n\n**RED**\n```typescript\ntest(''rejects empty email'', async () => {\n  const result = await submitForm({ email: '''' });\n  expect(result.error).toBe(''Email required'');\n});\n```\n\n**Verify RED**\n```bash\n$ npm test\nFAIL: expected ''Email required'', got undefined\n```\n\n**GREEN**\n```typescript\nfunction submitForm(data: FormData) {\n  if (!data.email?.trim()) {\n    return { error: ''Email required'' };\n  }\n  // ...\n}\n```\n\n**Verify GREEN**\n```bash\n$ npm test\nPASS\n```\n\n**REFACTOR**\nExtract validation for multiple fields if needed.\n\n## Verification Checklist\n\nBefore marking work complete:\n\n- [ ] Every new function/method has a test\n- [ ] Watched each test fail before implementing\n- [ ] Each test failed for expected reason (feature missing, not typo)\n- [ ] Wrote minimal code to pass each test\n- [ ] All tests pass\n- [ ] Output pristine (no errors, warnings)\n- [ ] Tests use real code (mocks only if unavoidable)\n- [ ] Edge cases and errors covered\n\nCan''t check all boxes? You skipped TDD. Start over.\n\n## When Stuck\n\n| Problem | Solution |\n|---------|----------|\n| Don''t know how to test | Write wished-for API. Write assertion first. Ask your human partner. |\n| Test too complicated | Design too complicated. Simplify interface. |\n| Must mock everything | Code too coupled. Use dependency injection. |\n| Test setup huge | Extract helpers. Still complex? Simplify design. |\n\n## Debugging Integration\n\nBug found? Write failing test reproducing it. Follow TDD cycle. Test proves fix and prevents regression.\n\nNever fix bugs without a test.\n\n## Testing Anti-Patterns\n\nWhen adding mocks or test utilities, read @testing-anti-patterns.md to avoid common pitfalls:\n- Testing mock behavior instead of real behavior\n- Adding test-only methods to production classes\n- Mocking without understanding dependencies\n\n## Final Rule\n\n```\nProduction code → test exists and failed first\nOtherwise → not TDD\n```\n\nNo exceptions without your human partner''s permission.\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-03-06T03:35:19.586Z","seo":{"title":{"en":"Test-Driven Development: Best Practices for AI Agents | A...","es":"Guía de configuración de Desarrollo Dirigido por Pruebas ...","fr":"Guide de mise en place du Développement Piloté par les Te...","de":"Einrichtungsleitfaden für testgetriebene Entwicklung (TDD...","pt":"Guia de Configuração de Desenvolvimento Dirigido por Test...","ru":"Настройка Инструментов ИИ для Test-Driven Development (TD...","ar":"دليل إعداد التطوير الموجه بالاختبار (TDD) لأدوات الذكاء ا..."},"description":{"en":"Learn how to implement test-driven development for new features, bug fixes, and refactoring. Get started with TDD today and improve your code quality!","es":"Aprenda a implementar TDD en sus proyectos de desarrollo de software con agentes de IA. Mejore la calidad y reduzca errores con pruebas automatizadas","fr":"Découvrez comment mettre en place le TDD dans vos projets de développement logiciel avec des outils d''IA. Améliorez la qualité et réduisez les erreurs avec d...","de":"Erfahren Sie, wie Sie TDD in Ihre Software-Entwicklungsprojekte mit KI-Agents integrieren können. Verbessern Sie die Qualität und reduzieren Sie Fehler mit a...","pt":"Aprenda a implementar o desenvolvimento dirigido por testes (TDD) em seus projetos de IA com nossa guia passo a passo","ru":"Узнайте, как настроить тестирование Инструментов ИИ с помощью TDD и улучшить качество своего кода","ar":"تعلم كيفية تطبيق التطوير الموجه بالاختبار (TDD) في مشاريعك الخاصة بالذكاء الاصطناعي مع دليلنا الشامل"},"definition":{"en":"Test-driven development is a software development process that relies on the repetitive cycle of writing tests before writing implementation code.","es":"TDD es una técnica de desarrollo de software que implica escribir pruebas antes de implementar el código para garantizar la calidad","fr":"TDD est une technique de développement logiciel qui consiste à écrire des tests avant de mettre en œuvre le code pour garantir la qualité","de":"TDD ist eine Software-Entwicklungstechnik, bei der Tests vor der Implementierung des Codes geschrieben werden, um die Qualität zu gewährleisten","pt":"TDD é uma abordagem de desenvolvimento de software que envolve escrever testes antes de escrever o código.","ru":"TDD - это подход к разработке программного обеспечения, при котором сначала пишутся тесты.","ar":"TDD هو نهج في تطوير البرمجيات يتضمن كتابة الاختبارات قبل كتابة الشفرة."},"features":{"en":["Writes tests before implementation code","Ensures code quality through repetitive test cycles","Supports new features, bug fixes, and refactoring","Requires minimal code to pass tests","Validates test effectiveness by watching tests fail","Excludes throwaway prototypes and generated code from TDD"],"es":["Escribe pruebas antes de implementar el código","Garantiza la calidad y reduce errores","Se aplica a nuevas características, correcciones de errores y refactorización","Excepciones para prototipos descartables, código generado y archivos de configuración","Requiere ver el fallo de la prueba para asegurarse de que se prueba lo correcto"],"fr":["Écrivez des tests avant de mettre en œuvre le code","Garantit la qualité et réduit les erreurs","S''applique aux nouvelles fonctionnalités, corrections de bogues et refactoring","Exceptions pour les prototypes jetables, code généré et fichiers de configuration","Nécessite de voir l''échec du test pour s''assurer que l''on teste la bonne chose"],"de":["Schreiben Sie Tests vor der Implementierung des Codes","Gewährleistet die Qualität und reduziert Fehler","Wird auf neue Funktionen, Fehlerkorrekturen und Refactoring angewendet","Ausnahmen für verworfene Prototypen, generierten Code und Konfigurationsdateien","Erfordert das Anzeigen des Testfehlers, um sicherzustellen, dass das Richtige getestet wird"],"pt":["Escreva testes antes de escrever o código de implementação","Verifique se o teste falha antes de escrever o código","Escreva o código mínimo necessário para passar no teste","Refatore o código para melhorar a legibilidade e a manutenção","Aplicar TDD em novos recursos, correções de bugs e refatoração"],"ru":["Пишите тесты до написания кода реализации","Смотрите, как тест失败ает перед написанием кода","Пишите минимальный код, необходимый для прохождения теста","Рефакторите код для улучшения читаемости и обслуживания","Применяйте TDD для новых функций, исправления ошибок и рефакторинга"],"ar":["اكتب الاختبارات قبل كتابة رمز التنفيذ","تحقق من فشل الاختبار قبل كتابة الرمز","اكتب رمز الحد الأدنى اللازم للنجاح في الاختبار","إعادة هيكلة الرمز لتحسين القراءة والصيانة","تطبيق TDD على الميزات الجديدة وتصحيح الأخطاء وإعادة الهيكلة"]},"keywords":{"en":["how to use test-driven development","what is test-driven development","test-driven development best practices","test-driven development vs behavior-driven development","test-driven development setup guide","test-driven development for AI agents","implementing test-driven development for new features","test-driven development for bug fixes and refactoring"],"es":["desarrollo dirigido por pruebas","TDD","pruebas automatizadas","calidad del software","reducción de errores","agentes de IA","herramientas de IA","desarrollo de software","pruebas unitarias","pruebas de integración"],"fr":["développement piloté par les tests","TDD","tests automatisés","qualité logicielle","réduction des erreurs","outils d''IA","développement logiciel","tests unitaires","tests d''intégration"],"de":["testgetriebene Entwicklung","TDD","automatisierte Tests","Software-Qualität","Fehlerreduzierung","KI-Agents","Software-Entwicklung","Einheitstests","Integrations-tests"],"pt":["desenvolvimento dirigido por testes","TDD","testes unitários","desenvolvimento de software","ferramentas de IA","programação","codificação","testes automatizados"],"ru":["тестирование","TDD","инструменты ИИ","разработка программного обеспечения","программирование","кодирование","автоматизированное тестирование","ИИ агенты"],"ar":["التطوير الموجه بالاختبار","TDD","اختبارات الوحدة","تطوير البرمجيات","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","برمجة","كتابة الشفرة","اختبارات آلية","وكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Agents specializing in software development lifecycle automation, particularly those focused on code quality assurance and regression prevention.","zh":"非常适合专门从事软件开发生命周期自动化的AI代理，特别是那些专注于代码质量保证和回归防止的代理。","ja":"ソフトウェア開発ライフサイクル自動化に特化したAIエージェント、特にコード品質保証と回帰防止に焦点を当てたものにとって最適です。","ko":"소프트웨어 개발 生命周期 자동화를 전문으로 하는 AI 에이전트, 특히 코드 품질 보증 및 회귀 방지에 중점을 둔 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de IA especializados en la automatización del ciclo de vida del desarrollo de software, especialmente aquellos enfocados en la garantía de calidad del código y la prevención de regresiones.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''IA spécialisés dans l''automatisation du cycle de vie du développement logiciel, en particulier ceux axés sur l''assurance qualité du code et la prévention des régressions.","de":"Perfekt für KI-Agenten, die sich auf die Automatisierung des Softwareentwicklungslebenszyklus spezialisiert haben, insbesondere auf die Qualitätssicherung von Code und die Verhinderung von Regressionen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA especializados na automação do ciclo de vida de desenvolvimento de software, particularmente aqueles focados na garantia de qualidade de código e prevenção de regressão.","ru":"Идеально подходит для ИИ-агентов, специализирующихся на автоматизации жизненного цикла разработки программного обеспечения, особенно тех, которые ориентированы на обеспечение качества кода и предотвращение регрессии.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي المتخصصين في أتمتة دورة حياة تطوير البرمجيات، وخاصة أولئك الذين يركزون على ضمان جودة الكود ومنع التراجع."},"recommendation":{"en":"Enables agents to implement features and bug fixes with guaranteed correctness by requiring test creation before implementation code. This ensures every change is verified against specifications and prevents regression errors from being introduced.","zh":"使代理能够通过在实现代码之前创建测试来实现功能和错误修复，并确保每次更改都经过验证，以防止回归错误的引入。","ja":"実装コード前にテストを作成することで、エージェントが機能とバグ修正を確実に正しく実装できるようにし、すべての変更が仕様に対して検証されることを保証し、回帰エラーの導入を防ぐ。","ko":"구현 코드 전에 테스트를 만들어서 에이전트가 기능 및 버그 수정을 확실하게 올바르게 구현할 수 있도록 하며 모든 변경 사항이 사양에 대해 검증되도록 보장하고 회귀 오류의 도입을 방지합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes implementar características y correcciones de errores con garantía de corrección al requerir la creación de pruebas antes del código de implementación. Esto asegura que cada cambio sea verificado contra las especificaciones y previene que se introduzcan errores de regresión.","fr":"Permet aux agents de mettre en œuvre des fonctionnalités et des corrections de bogues avec une exactitude garantie en exigeant la création de tests avant le code d''implémentation. Cela garantit que chaque changement est vérifié par rapport aux spécifications et empêche l''introduction d''erreurs de régression.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Funktionen und Fehlerbehebungen mit garantierter Korrektheit zu implementieren, indem die Erstellung von Tests vor dem Implementierungscode erforderlich ist. Dies stellt sicher, dass jede Änderung gegen Spezifikationen verifiziert wird und verhindert, dass Regressionsfehler eingeführt werden.","pt":"Permite que os agentes implementem funcionalidades e correções de bugs com correção garantida, exigindo a criação de testes antes do código de implementação. Isso garante que cada alteração seja verificada em relação às especificações e evita que erros de regressão sejam introduzidos.","ru":"Позволяет агентам реализовывать функции и исправления ошибок с гарантированной корректностью, требуя создания тестов до кода реализации. Это гарантирует, что каждое изменение проверяется в соответствии со спецификациями и предотвращает внесение регрессионных ошибок.","ar":"يمكن الوكلاء من تنفيذ الميزات وإصلاحات الأخطاء مع ضمان الصحة من خلال اشتراط إنشاء الاختبارات قبل كود التنفيذ. وهذا يضمن التحقق من كل تغيير مقابل المواصفات ويمنع إدخال أخطاء التراجع."},"useCases":{"en":["Implementing new features with built-in verification","Fixing bugs with regression protection","Refactoring code with safety guarantees","Validating behavior changes against requirements"],"zh":["带有内置验证的新功能实现","带有回归保护的错误修复","带有安全保障的代码重构","行为更改的验证"],"ja":["組み込みの検証を備えた新機能の実装","回帰保護を備えたバグ修正","安全性の保証のあるコードのリファクタリング","要件に対する動作の変更の検証"],"ko":["내장 확인을 갖춘 새로운 기능 구현","회귀 보호를 갖춘 버그 수정","안전 보장을 갖춘 코드 리팩토링","요구 사항에 대한 동작 변경의 확인"],"es":["Implementar nuevas características con verificación incorporada","Corregir errores con protección contra regresiones","Refactorizar código con garantías de seguridad","Validar cambios de comportamiento contra requisitos"],"fr":["Mise en œuvre de nouvelles fonctionnalités avec vérification intégrée","Correction de bogues avec protection contre la régression","Refactorisation du code avec garanties de sécurité","Validation des changements de comportement par rapport aux exigences"],"de":["Implementieren neuer Funktionen mit integrierter Verifikation","Beheben von Fehlern mit Regressionsschutz","Refaktorisieren von Code mit Sicherheitsgarantien","Validieren von Verhaltensänderungen gegen Anforderungen"],"pt":["Implementar novas funcionalidades com verificação incorporada","Corrigir bugs com proteção contra regressão","Refatorar código com garantias de segurança","Validar mudanças de comportamento em relação aos requisitos"],"ru":["Реализация новых функций со встроенной проверкой","Исправление ошибок с защитой от регрессии","Рефакторинг кода с гарантиями безопасности","Проверка изменений поведения в соответствии с требованиями"],"ar":["تنفيذ ميزات جديدة مع التحقق المدمج","إصلاح الأخطاء مع حماية من التراجع","إعادة هيكلة الكود مع ضمانات السلامة","التحقق من صحة تغييرات السلوك مقابل المتطلبات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires comprehensive test suite maintenance","Not suitable for throwaway prototypes or generated code","Adds development time overhead for initial implementation"],"zh":["需要综合测试套件维护","不适合一次性原型或生成代码","增加初始实现的开发时间开销"],"ja":["包括的なテストスイートのメンテナンスが必要","使い捨てのプロトタイプや生成されたコードには適さない","初期実装の開発時間のオーバーヘッドを追加"],"ko":["포괄적인 테스트套件 유지 관리가 필요합니다.","일회용 프로토 타입 또는 생성 된 코드에 적합하지 않습니다.","초기 구현의 개발 시간 오버 헤드가 추가됩니다."],"es":["Requiere mantenimiento integral de la suite de pruebas","No es adecuado para prototipos desechables o código generado","Añade sobrecarga de tiempo de desarrollo para la implementación inicial"],"fr":["Nécessite une maintenance complète de la suite de tests","Ne convient pas aux prototypes jetables ou au code généré","Ajoute une surcharge de temps de développement pour la mise en œuvre initiale"],"de":["Erfordert umfassende Wartung des Test-Suites","Nicht geeignet für Wegwerfprototypen oder generierten Code","Fügt Overhead an Entwicklungszeit für die Erstimplementierung hinzu"],"pt":["Requer manutenção abrangente do conjunto de testes","Não é adequado para protótipos descartáveis ou código gerado","Adiciona sobrecarga de tempo de desenvolvimento para a implementação inicial"],"ru":["Требует комплексного обслуживания набора тестов","Не подходит для одноразовых прототипов или сгенерированного кода","Добавляет накладные расходы по времени разработки для первоначальной реализации"],"ar":["يتطلب صيانة شاملة لمجموعة الاختبارات","غير مناسب للنماذج الأولية التي تستخدم لمرة واحدة أو الكود المُنشَأ","يضيف عبئًا إضافيًا على وقت التطوير للتنفيذ الأولي"]},"version":4},"contentHash":"7dee67b4af6bdccc7a914ca34533184d64592d0f5b23aeae631538168db14994","repoEtag":"W/\"a8a266458ca9bbf6c9312a7647f733e0f1891eedfa2dde0bddcec7f7d186089e\"","qualityScore":86}');
